1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,291
In the deepest shadows of St Andrews
University library in Scotland, hidden

2
00:00:07,311 --> 00:00:14,123
away in a dark, forgotten corner, sits a
16th-century leather tome.

3
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:20,113
Its cover is cracked, weathered, and
blackened by centuries of damp air.

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:25,450
On the inside of the back cover, an artist
in the year

5
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:30,790
1578 drew a picture that makes the heart
turn cold.

6
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:35,380
It depicts a towering, skeletal man with
long, gaunt

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:40,155
limbs, standing at the edge of a twisting
forest.

8
00:00:40,175 --> 00:00:45,181
Veins bulge across his pale, hairless
skull, his dark

9
00:00:45,201 --> 00:00:49,828
eyes are sunken deep within bone, and
beneath the

10
00:00:49,848 --> 00:00:54,491
ink is written a single name: Herbert
Solomon.

11
00:00:54,511 --> 00:00:58,228
Let us go back to the winter where this
nightmare began.

12
00:00:58,828 --> 00:01:04,516
The book chronicles the isolated town of
Ettrick, set amidst the

13
00:01:04,536 --> 00:01:10,168
bleak moorlands and dense pine forests of
southern Scotland.

14
00:01:10,188 --> 00:01:14,598
In the freezing December of 1577, an
unspeakable

15
00:01:14,618 --> 00:01:19,016
dread settled over the cobblestone
streets.

16
00:01:19,036 --> 00:01:23,154
The first to disappear was young Alana
Sutherland.

17
00:01:23,174 --> 00:01:29,082
She had dropped her hand-carved doll down
an old stone well on the edge

18
00:01:29,102 --> 00:01:35,060
of town, and returned at sunset with a
hook and rope to retrieve it.

19
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,021
She was never seen again.

20
00:01:37,041 --> 00:01:40,921
Days later, another child vanished while
walking

21
00:01:40,941 --> 00:01:44,552
an errand just two streets from his home.

22
00:01:44,572 --> 00:01:49,821
By late January, seven children had been
torn from existence.

23
00:01:49,841 --> 00:01:54,475
Fear consumed every cottage, turning
neighbor against neighbor.

24
00:01:55,075 --> 00:01:58,687
When two more children vanished in
mid-February,

25
00:01:58,707 --> 00:02:02,317
the desperate town elder demanded a
culprit.

26
00:02:02,337 --> 00:02:07,032
In every house and across every church
pew, one whisper

27
00:02:07,052 --> 00:02:11,254
grew into a deafening roar: Herbert
Solomon.

28
00:02:11,274 --> 00:02:14,995
Solomon was an outsider who lived in a
small

29
00:02:15,015 --> 00:02:19,036
wooden cabin deep within the Ettrick
forest.

30
00:02:19,056 --> 00:02:25,743
Ravaged by an unknown wasting disease, his
body was emaciated, his skin

31
00:02:25,763 --> 00:02:32,617
sheet-white, and he covered his face with
a tarnished hat and cloth.

32
00:02:32,637 --> 00:02:36,469
He would watch the village children play
from the tree line.

33
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:43,633
On several occasions, children returned
home carrying exquisitely carved wooden

34
00:02:43,653 --> 00:02:50,099
dolls and toys—left on tree stumps as
gifts from the gentle recluse.

35
00:02:50,119 --> 00:02:53,660
But to fearful parents, this was proof of
evil.

36
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:59,767
On a freezing February night, grief and
hatred reached a boiling pitch.

37
00:02:59,787 --> 00:03:06,741
Decreeing Solomon a child-killing
abomination, a mob of villagers armed

38
00:03:06,761 --> 00:03:13,969
with axes, scythes, and flaming torches
marched into the dark forest.

39
00:03:13,989 --> 00:03:20,033
They surrounded his humble cabin and
barred the heavy timbers from outside.

40
00:03:20,053 --> 00:03:26,817
Cheering in a frenzy of revenge, they
tossed torches onto the dried thatched

41
00:03:26,837 --> 00:03:32,890
roof and watched the cabin ignite into a
wall of roaring flame.

42
00:03:32,910 --> 00:03:37,981
Solomon's desperate screams echoed through
the Scots pines,

43
00:03:38,001 --> 00:03:42,510
before fading into the crackle of falling
timber.

44
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:47,009
Satisfied that justice was served, the mob
returned

45
00:03:47,029 --> 00:03:50,293
home, convinced the curse was lifted.

46
00:03:50,893 --> 00:03:55,418
Yet within days, a suffocating fog
descended over

47
00:03:55,438 --> 00:03:59,984
Ettrick, and terror returned with a
vengeance.

48
00:04:00,004 --> 00:04:04,514
Townsfolk began waking in the dead of
night to the sound

49
00:04:04,534 --> 00:04:09,008
of floorboards creaking under an unnatural
weight.

50
00:04:09,028 --> 00:04:15,383
An elderly woman woke to rustling beneath
her bed, watching in paralyzed

51
00:04:15,403 --> 00:04:21,526
horror as a tall, skeletal figure dragged
itself across the floor.

52
00:04:21,546 --> 00:04:26,534
In a cellar, a tradesman encountered the
gaunt, sheet-white

53
00:04:26,554 --> 00:04:30,380
phantom hunched beneath the low rafters.

54
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:34,418
Then, the impossible occurred: an orphan
girl was

55
00:04:34,438 --> 00:04:38,591
snatched screaming from the foggy
cobblestones.

56
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:42,725
Days later, another child vanished from
his bedroom.

57
00:04:42,745 --> 00:04:48,132
Even inside the parish church, Solomon's
tall, spindly shadow

58
00:04:48,152 --> 00:04:52,672
stepped into the aisle before dissolving
into mist.

59
00:04:53,272 --> 00:04:59,862
Believing Solomon's vengeful wraith had
returned to punish the town, Vicar

60
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:05,758
McKenzie assembled a group of chosen men
armed with blessed steel,

61
00:05:05,778 --> 00:05:12,103
flaming torches, and vials of holy water
to hunt the phantom down.

62
00:05:12,123 --> 00:05:17,934
They waited in the midnight mist until the
solitary figure of Herbert

63
00:05:17,954 --> 00:05:23,895
Solomon appeared, walking the cobblestones
with purposeful strides.

64
00:05:23,915 --> 00:05:29,686
McKenzie and his men encircled the
creature, brandishing weapons.

65
00:05:29,706 --> 00:05:34,761
The vicar splashed holy water across the
stone, and a torch

66
00:05:34,781 --> 00:05:39,964
struck Solomon's sleeve, setting the
frayed cloth alight.

67
00:05:39,984 --> 00:05:44,382
But the tall figure broke through the
circle, fleeing like

68
00:05:44,402 --> 00:05:48,363
a giant spider shadow across the village
courtyards.

69
00:05:48,963 --> 00:05:53,337
Pursued by the shouting mob, Solomon
sprinted down the

70
00:05:53,357 --> 00:05:57,869
main street and ducked into an open
cottage doorway.

71
00:05:57,889 --> 00:06:02,448
McKenzie and the villagers burst inside,
only to find

72
00:06:02,468 --> 00:06:07,476
a weak, trembling young girl lying on the
hall floor.

73
00:06:07,496 --> 00:06:12,191
With her last ounce of strength, the child
pointed toward

74
00:06:12,211 --> 00:06:16,958
the stone stairway and whispered a single
word: Below.

75
00:06:16,978 --> 00:06:21,371
The vicar descended with his torch into
the cold cellar

76
00:06:21,391 --> 00:06:25,272
vault, and the breath caught in his
throat.

77
00:06:25,292 --> 00:06:29,709
Chained against the damp stone walls were
the missing

78
00:06:29,729 --> 00:06:33,943
children—malnourished and terrified, but
alive!

79
00:06:33,963 --> 00:06:39,719
And lying motionless upon the stone floor
was the true fiend: Tom

80
00:06:39,739 --> 00:06:45,857
Sutherland, the father of the very first
child who had vanished.

81
00:06:45,877 --> 00:06:50,564
Sutherland had killed his daughter in a
drunken rage, and

82
00:06:50,584 --> 00:06:55,075
consumed by madness, had stolen the other
children.

83
00:06:55,095 --> 00:07:00,978
He was about to execute another captive
when Herbert Solomon burst through

84
00:07:00,998 --> 00:07:06,901
the cellar door, ending Sutherland's reign
of terror to save the innocent.

85
00:07:07,501 --> 00:07:12,675
The town rejoiced, realizing with heavy
shame that the gentle

86
00:07:12,695 --> 00:07:18,084
recluse they had burned alive was their
protector all along.

87
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:22,388
Yet the story does not end in the 16th
century.

88
00:07:22,408 --> 00:07:27,193
Centuries later, while researching the
Ettrick tome, I visited

89
00:07:27,213 --> 00:07:31,136
a colleague's estate near the Scottish
borders.

90
00:07:31,156 --> 00:07:37,446
The following afternoon, panicked screams
shattered the tranquil countryside—my

91
00:07:37,466 --> 00:07:43,168
friend's little daughter had fallen into a
violent, swollen river.

92
00:07:43,188 --> 00:07:47,137
Swept by torrential currents toward jagged
rocks,

93
00:07:47,157 --> 00:07:51,325
the child lost her grip on a slippery tree
root.

94
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:55,477
We plunged into the rapids, but we were
too far away.

95
00:07:55,497 --> 00:07:57,725
She was seconds from drowning.

96
00:07:57,745 --> 00:08:00,609
Suddenly, the forest branches cracked.

97
00:08:00,629 --> 00:08:07,552
From the opposite bank, a tall, gaunt
figure burst forth at superhuman speed.

98
00:08:07,572 --> 00:08:11,953
A long, skeletal hand plunged deep into
the churning

99
00:08:11,973 --> 00:08:15,788
foam, pulling the girl gently to safety.

100
00:08:15,808 --> 00:08:22,021
The pale, withered man placed the child on
the grass, gazed across the

101
00:08:22,041 --> 00:08:28,287
river with dark, sorrowful eyes, and
vanished into the Scots pines.

102
00:08:28,307 --> 00:08:35,090
Even in death, Herbert Solomon was the
kindest and gentlest of souls.

103
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:38,731
This story was adapted from Scottish
folklore

104
00:08:38,751 --> 00:08:41,932
and the legend of Herbert Solomon.

105
00:08:41,952 --> 00:08:43,162
Now tell me.

106
00:08:43,182 --> 00:08:45,612
Would you have judged him by his face?

